{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay","id":989861,"title":"Too many rules too few roleplay?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-19T07:21:47-07:00","id":989861,"title":"Too many rules too few roleplay?","content":"I had been thinking about it from some time and finally i decided to open a thread about it:<br /> <br /> with second edition a lot of new rules were introduced, rules that i find not only unneeded but even harmfull for a roleplaying game. The game itself is very complex with how spells work and that's part of the fun, i don't really see the need for even more complex rules to encourage/force players to play.<br /> Roleplay becomes a mechanic that is even rewarded mechanically with exp: obsessions are just a way to keep control of players and force them to do things that are compatible with the narrator storyline, i can see how this can help gamists and inexperienced narrators but i think that is a way to transform a roleplaying game into a boardgame, more on the subject conditions and tilts... seriously how are needed 10 pages of those things? to keep track you even have cards... and the game promotes you to use those conditions and tilts to exploit for exp.<br /> To play by the book a scene you have to start piling condition cards (maybe it's raining and it's dark, maybe one or more characters have some spells running), then players start to think that they have to do something because they have an obsession... then comes the social conflict rule system... Seriously what's the need of an in depth rule system to decide the outcome of roleplay? A character needs to convince someone and to do so what he does? start rolling diece... a chance to roleplay becomes a chance to roll dice. Since your character is good at speaking you can brain off and let dice do the talking...<br /> <br /> the new rules encourage players to look at their character sheets and start to think how to wombo combo things to get exp, they have to play their obsession to get exp, they have to cause disadvantages to themselves to get exp and so on, if they manage to do both at the same time win!<br /> characters are defined by their virtue/vices, their path, their order and now by obsessions, in the end it seems like they are constructed in such a way that every roleplaying moment is a consequence of a mechanic and not the real reason why you play in the first place.<br /> While playing i find myself telling to my players: ignore this, ignore that, don't worry about this, don't worry about that... practically all those new things are so mechanical and heavy on the game that i find myself playing using only the new rules for spells! And the worst part is that it forces us to house rule a lot! all those new mechanics are not optional but are integrated so deeply in the new system that not using them and wanting to actually roleplay is penalized.<br /> <br /> I am not against rulesystems, i feel the need for rules to avoid too much arbitrary decisions and to give players a solid idea of what they can accomplish, but i don't like when a game becomes more a series of rules than a roleplaying experience.<br /> Am i the only one feeling that this new course of cod is going too much on the gamist side of the spectrum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7038-nirgal","name":"Nirgal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T07:41:21-07:00","id":989867,"title":"","content":"I definitely don't feel that way. All of the Aspirations and Obsessions and Virtues/Vices and Conditions/Tilts and such are things I already did/wanted to do in a game. And now I'm <i>rewarded</i> for it! People don't get mad when I resolve a negative Condition because 1) it makes things more interesting for me and everybody else and 2) it gets me XP. They're doing the same thing. Same thing when I downgrade a Failure to a Dramatic Failure. Or when I screw over somebody else to pursue my Obsessions.<br /> <br /> The rules and systems help reinforce a certain tone, and can make things like PC vs PC less personal. I prefer my systems to be very integrated into the roleplaying, and games like CofD 2E are great for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T07:55:42-07:00","id":989872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=989867#post989867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely don't feel that way. All of the Aspirations and Obsessions and Virtues/Vices and Conditions/Tilts and such are things I already did/wanted to do in a game. And now I'm <i>rewarded</i> for it! People don't get mad when I resolve a negative Condition because 1) it makes things more interesting for me and everybody else and 2) it gets me XP. They're doing the same thing. Same thing when I downgrade a Failure to a Dramatic Failure. Or when I screw over somebody else to pursue my Obsessions.<br /> <br /> The rules and systems help reinforce a certain tone, and can make things like PC vs PC less personal. I prefer my systems to be very integrated into the roleplaying, and games like CofD 2E are great for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agree, every word.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T07:58:03-07:00","id":989873,"title":"","content":"Obsessions and Aspirations are ways for the player to tell the Storyteller what they want for their character.<br /> <br /> Conditions and Tilts are just a fancy name for Effects, and offer players incentives for playing them up. The only difference between, 'You've been blinded by the flash,' and 'The flash is so bright it blinds you, take the Blinded Condition,' is that you can get experience from the latter. You don't need to pile up Condition cards. 'It's dark and rainy, take a -3 on your attempt to shoot the thug.'<br /> <br /> If you're worried about people trying to get more Beats for themselves than others, then use group Beats. They shouldn't have to cause disadvantages to themselves just to get Experience, but alternatively without Beats they have no reason to ever do anything that might be disadvantageous. In this form, Beats give you a reason to take risks with your character, because even if you fail you get a Beat, as opposed to a failure offering nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T07:59:52-07:00","id":989874,"title":"","content":"<b>Aspirations and Obsessions</b><br /> <br /> I think these are a great addition to the game. These are neatly divided into long and short-term goals that give information to the Storyteller. What are the players interested in? How are they going to go about fulfilling these goals? What are they aiming at in the short-term (this or the next session) or in the long-term (half a dozen to a dozen sessions from now)? I ask my players to create a storyline of their own. I know...how unorthodox of me to think that players might be interested in telling their own stories inside the giant sandbox that I have lovingly crafted for them. I do have my own stories to tell as a Storyteller, but most of the time I just listen to my players and let them direct the chronicle, while I keep dropping hints about something grander in the background. Sooner or later, the players also become increasingly interested in the stories I have, but I find it very desirable to get players invested in my chronicles. And nothing builds that better than allowing for personalized stories where the player characters play a central role.<br /> <br /> <b>Condition Cards and Tilts</b><br /> <br /> Honestly, I think these are mostly just a way to provide guidance and direction to less experienced players. I use them sparingly, because they can become a pointless hassle, if I just start throwing them around willy-nilly. Like any game mechanic they can become an obstacle rather than a good thing. Personally I haven't found them to be a problem and they do provide a little bit of extra guidance.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of what you are saying comes down to the fact that Mage 2E is a new thing. I have only run a few sessions myself, and it is a lot to take in. That's why I spent over an hour with all of my players just teaching them how the new magic system works. And I'm slowly introducing them to the rest of it. I think a lot of the ideas in the book are perfectly fine, but they do take time to get used to. The end result is, IMO, better than 1E. However, having only run a few sessions I reserve my right to change my mind later on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T08:15:23-07:00","id":989883,"title":"","content":"I can't say for others, but no. I disagree with you. I personally feel that having a system designed to reward dramatic roleplaying is actually the direct opposite of &quot;gamist.&quot; The game is actually changed in such a way that you can't advance as a character if you use a so-called gamist mindset. You get rewarded for failing, you get rewarded for making yourself vulnerable, you get rewarded for helping others succeed at their goals. In fact, the game is designed to mechanically reward Narrativist and Simulationist style of gameplay. In fact, the CofD is not the first game to go this route, but the system for rewarding experience for roleplaying is still rare. Its more rules-heavy, perhaps, than you are used to, but that is different from &quot;gamist&quot; mindset. Perhaps you are opposed to having a large amount of rules.<br /> <br /> I have to question a certain line. &quot;Then players start to think that they have to do something because they have an obsession.&quot; Yes, that's kind of the idea. Its called a plot hook. Characters having individual needs and drives that push them to do more than passively respond to a GM story, usually a combat threat, is usually considered a good thing by most people. Obsessions are really nothing more than a glorified Aspiration, and aspirations are just character goals by another name. <br /> <br /> You said that every action is a consequence of a mechanic rather than &quot;reason you started playing.&quot; People all play for different reasons and get different things out of the game. And I think its awesome that you get xp for playing for the reason you started playing? If I want to play an occult detective, isn't it awesome that I'm getting xp for doing that instead of just xp for fighting monsters? And if I want to get xp for fighting monsters, I can do that too. I think you've fallen prey to the Stormwind Fallacy. You can both get strong, and have fun roleplaying. In fact, the system is designed to encourage both at the same time. That's pretty cool.<br /> <br /> And, yes, I think Social Maneuvering is fun too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T08:20:01-07:00","id":989887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TelperionST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=989874#post989874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Aspirations and Obsessions</b><br /> <br /> I think these are a great addition to the game. These are neatly divided into long and short-term goals that give information to the Storyteller. What are the players interested in? How are they going to go about fulfilling these goals? What are they aiming at in the short-term (this or the next session) or in the long-term (half a dozen to a dozen sessions from now)? I ask my players to create a storyline of their own. I know...how unorthodox of me to think that players might be interested in telling their own stories inside the giant sandbox that I have lovingly crafted for them. I do have my own stories to tell as a Storyteller, but most of the time I just listen to my players and let them direct the chronicle, while I keep dropping hints about something grander in the background. Sooner or later, the players also become increasingly interested in the stories I have, but I find it very desirable to get players invested in my chronicles. And nothing builds that better than allowing for personalized stories where the player characters play a central role.<br /> <br /> <b>Condition Cards and Tilts</b><br /> <br /> Honestly, I think these are mostly just a way to provide guidance and direction to less experienced players. I use them sparingly, because they can become a pointless hassle, if I just start throwing them around willy-nilly. Like any game mechanic they can become an obstacle rather than a good thing. Personally I haven't found them to be a problem and they do provide a little bit of extra guidance.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of what you are saying comes down to the fact that Mage 2E is a new thing. I have only run a few sessions myself, and it is a lot to take in. That's why I spent over an hour with all of my players just teaching them how the new magic system works. And I'm slowly introducing them to the rest of it. I think a lot of the ideas in the book are perfectly fine, but they do take time to get used to. The end result is, IMO, better than 1E. However, having only run a few sessions I reserve my right to change my mind later on.</div> </div> </div> </div>my problem with obsessions is exactly that! a mechanic that enforces something that should be roleplay. A narrator should be able to tailor the story to the characters and make players involved, if this is left to a mechanic it's like playing a computer game. If a player roleplays his character there's no need for mechanics to incentive him to do what he is supposed to do, in anycase you write down a background (or anyway make it up) and surely you are going to talk with the narrator about who you are, so using obsessions to tell the narrator those things is just pointless. More importantly obsessions force players to act in a certain way just like virtues and vices and to some extent path/order, while path and order are roleplaying boundries or directions vices/virtues are both mechanical and rolplaying, obsessions too are mechanical but really lack the roleplay part because they are &quot;what you are supposed to do&quot;.<br /> When you make things more difficult on purpouse to gain exp you are metagaming, everytime you do something to gain a mechanical benefit you are metagaiming and i strongly belive that metagame should be avoided as much as possible. My point is that too much of the new rules are about metagaming in one way or another (social conflict rules are possibly the worst part but they can be ignored without much trouble). If a player starts to think of how to gain exp he is stopping to roleplay, this is bound to happen in certain groups but what i don't like is the fact that the new rules encourage such thing and that's why my group avoids all those kind of rules.<br /> <br /> for conditions<br /> most games, even more complex systems, just have 1 page or at max 2 pages to describe an all purpouse system, going to such detail and anyway being forced to come up with some kind of not well defined rule force every possible case into the track seems to me a poor design, one that is not too much of a problem but more a sympthom of an approach to the game itself.<br /> just look at nimbus tilts... or at spell tilts... you have a system of 10 pages that rises more questions than what it answers and if you actually bother applying those rules your session will bog down to a trading card game tapping and tapping for mana is the next step.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7038-nirgal","name":"Nirgal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T08:36:00-07:00","id":989893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nirgal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=989887#post989887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">my problem with obsessions is exactly that! a mechanic that enforces something that should be roleplay.</div> </div> </div> </div> Why separate the two? It sounds like you're more upset that there are mechanics that reflect social influences on your character than anything else. Or that there are social mechanics at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T08:54:21-07:00","id":989902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nirgal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=989887#post989887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you make things more difficult on purpouse to gain exp you are metagaming, everytime you do something to gain a mechanical benefit you are metagaiming and i strongly belive that metagame should be avoided as much as possible. My point is that too much of the new rules are about metagaming in one way or another (social conflict rules are possibly the worst part but they can be ignored without much trouble). If a player starts to think of how to gain exp he is stopping to roleplay, this is bound to happen in certain groups but what i don't like is the fact that the new rules encourage such thing and that's why my group avoids all those kind of rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, okay, I think there's a difference in the way we think here, so I'm going to pick my brain and (possibly) give you a new idea. So, I'm all about the storytelling, hence I really like the Revised Storytelling System. Therefore, I don't have any problems with a player changing what a player character would do, or how the character might react to a situation, if it creates a more interesting story for everyone involved. <u>Even if that knowledge is not available to the player character at the present time.</u> So, in very literal sense I'm all for metagaming. I like it, because picking up on a cool idea that another player had creates superior stories. Or, if I, as a storyteller, have an idea then I have no problem with sharing my idea with the players. Now, to be fair, I don't give out full details about the stories that I have crafted, but I do encourage players to share their own stories in detail before they we run through them during sessions. This way players can get feedback on their ideas and improve on their personalize storylines. Not to mention that it's very rare that anything happens literally the same way that someone planned it. Does it take some of the surprise out of the gaming experience? Yes, but then again those personized stories are only a small fraction of the content that I, as a Storyteller, provide to my players.<br /> <br /> I found Nimbus Tilts to be really simple. A nice little bit of personalization. Spell Tilts...I haven't actually run into a lot of those yet outside of something like the Blinded Tilt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T09:10:03-07:00","id":989908,"title":"","content":"Everything <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2648_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2648\" data-vbnamecard=\"2648\">TelperionST</a> just said is spot on for me. I'm more interested in crafting a story than playing a game, so to speak. When I'm not rewarded for making things interesting, I feel dis-incentivized from doing interesting things or taking risks, whether they're in-character or not. In other words, when I don't get rewarded for the things I want to do I metagame <i>more</i> because I don't want to rock the boat or cause problems with my group.<br /> <br /> Also, think of Conditions and those things as a codification of what counts as &quot;Good Roleplaying.&quot; In CofD1E and all versions of WoD, there was that super-vague, super-unhelpful &quot;Reward players with XP for good roleplaying.&quot; It put that power in the hands of the ST and gave no guidance on what the hell that meant. CofD2E breaks it out into all sorts of stuff, mostly &quot;Be your character's worst enemy&quot;, &quot;Do things that push the narrative&quot;, and &quot;Introduce complications to the plot to be resolved&quot;. I think it's a far preferable alternative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T09:44:18-07:00","id":989921,"title":"","content":"point is that you should be incentivized in-game not out-of game, at least that is how i see it. Being clever, improving the story, creating interesting situations is part of what roleplaying means, if you play to get the sweety the entire focus of the game shifts from roleplaying to just playing, it's like playing a boardgame where you make choices not because you identify yourself with your character but because you have &quot;to win&quot;.<br /> We all are complex individuals and we do not act thinking: if i do this i will get exp! being part of a story means you identify yourself with your character and with the setting/story, if you start thinking outside your character you stop roleplaying. When you make your character drunk into stupor just before a fight why you do it? because your character is addicted to alchool and doesn't cope well with pressure or because you are going to get exp? When you write your character to be an alchoolic you give him that flaw for some exp or because you like the concept and want to play a drunkard?<br /> Rules are needed to put order and give structure to &quot;nature&quot;, you need rules to quantify how much your character has learned or how far he can jump, having rules that tell you what you are supposed to do or how a certain number on your character sheet will automatically let you sell an horse carcass as an airplane is like following a script and that defies the purpouse of roleplaying.<br /> <br /> the concept that you need mechanical rules to make you roleplay is a paradox because to follow those rules you have to metagame and thus stop roleplaying. everytime you make a decision for your character that is based on a metagame you are avoiding or possibly breaking the suspension of disbelif, thus you are transforming a narration into an equation.<br /> <br /> we all have our styles of play and all are legit if you have fun, the thing that i don't like is that this line (wod, nwod, cod) has lost much of the &quot;flavour&quot; it had, the WoD in his last days had become too d&amp;d for my tastes (setting wise, the ruleset was almost always the same) and with the nWoD i saw a good change of direction (or return to certain ways of exploring certain themes both in the setting and the system), now with CoD i feel that this line has become more and more gameist, founding the system on the assumption that players and narrators are really poor roleplayers that need to be forced to roleplay and in this attempt they make tons of rules that in the end strip most of the roleplay from the game itself.<br /> <br /> anyway i see that i'm the only one thinking this way XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7038-nirgal","name":"Nirgal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T09:51:56-07:00","id":989924,"title":"","content":"I'm curious, Nirgal. Have you ever tried playing without XP? Like, fill out a character sheet, and add random stuff whenever the ST says it's okay to, but just don't ever reward XP. For anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T09:53:17-07:00","id":989925,"title":"","content":"Do you often find yourself passing up the opportunity for your character to get a beat because it would have been out of character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T09:56:47-07:00","id":989927,"title":"","content":"I must admit when I went from 1e to 2e I was disappointed with how much fiddlier the system had become, and just how <i>dense </i>that rulebook is, especially as I was dealing with players totally new to nWoD. However, certain updates, Aspirations and Obsessions in particular, or the clarity of focus in Arcana, really quite pleased me and I stuck with the system. And I think the big problem is not that the rules don't lend themselves to roleplay, they absolutely do, it's just that it's not clear how you're meant to <i>use </i>those rules in story. Honestly it's taken me some time to realise that the game relies on proactive players and Aspirations are meant to be ways to encourage players to drop in their own scenes, rather than merely a list of &quot;to-do&quot; items the ST is meant to incorporate into the script of the plot, or that Mysteries are just &quot;mystical things your characters look into&quot; rather than &quot;esoteric equivalent of a whodunnit.&quot; Environmental Tilts to me are really the equivalent of traps in a D&amp;D dungeon, they're environmental set dressing that influence mechanics and often problems that need direct solving. If you don't want to focus on environment, you don't have to think too hard about them. <br /> <br /> I was talking to one of my players about this. They said Mage 2e was absolutely not their thing given its density and myriad rules, <i>except </i>they were still having a great time playing with it because I listened to what bits they found interesting and let them play with that. I think that's the core of it, is realising that Mage is meant to be more of a sandbox game taking place over weeks at a time. If players need Willpower they can come up with a scene where they act out a Vice, and you can portray those consequences. Ditto they can take time out to work on an Aspiration or an Obsession. They want to get something from Order contacts, great, that's a scene you can tie into a sequence as they're called back for favours. Indeed, realising that it's meant to be played over narrative rather than immediate time lets social maneuvering make actual sense, because you can let players build up relationships <i>over time, </i>rather than &quot;passing through, can I use your Hallow?&quot; But that realisation has honestly been a big conceptual breakthrough for how I ST my game.<br /> <br /> What I will say I don't like about Mage 2e is that it really, truly, requires players to be totally au fait with the lore, meaning they have to sit down with all those books to get a firm grip on what they want to do. There's no easy way for an ST to dump the required info into their laps without it breaking immersion, or to suggest ideas to them without feeling like you're railroading them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T10:02:54-07:00","id":989931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nirgal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=989921#post989921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">being part of a story means you identify yourself with your character and with the setting/story, if you start thinking outside your character you stop roleplaying.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> the concept that you need mechanical rules to make you roleplay is a paradox because to follow those rules you have to metagame and thus stop roleplaying. everytime you make a decision for your character that is based on a metagame you are avoiding or possibly breaking the suspension of disbelif, thus you are transforming a narration into an equation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to be much meaner in my response to these two lines, but I've cooled down a bit: let's just say I 100% disagree with you on these points. I don't play the game to win, I play the game to make interesting stories about people with strong drive and strong flaws. I want to be rewarded both in- and out-of-character whenever I push the narrative forward and inject dramatic complications into the plot.<br /> <br /> When I'm a player I'm creating the story as much as the Storyteller and I'm assuming the role of the author as much as the actor as much as the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T10:04:56-07:00","id":989934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=989924#post989924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious, Nirgal. Have you ever tried playing without XP? Like, fill out a character sheet, and add random stuff whenever the ST says it's okay to, but just don't ever reward XP. For anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>i reward exp by what i consider appropriate and considering how fast i want to make the players progress. i usually have the directive that what you earn in-game doesn't need exp coverage and what you get with exp needs in-game coverage, for ex: if you want a contact in the police departement go ahead and in-game find those contacts, if you find a way to achieve that you will get to write those contacts on your sheet; you want a safe place? go ahead and make arrangements, buy a house, find a good trusted security system installer etc; if you get a magical item in-game it's yours no need to spend exp to be able to use it.<br /> on the other hand if you get a magical object thx to exp you have to justify in-game why you have it, often such things are possible in the &quot;downtime&quot; between two stories or chapters.<br /> <br /> i award exp for partecipating in events (you always learn at least something), for creative thinking or for anything that moves the story forward, for the introduction of interesting elements or even sidestories, for playing your character above the average making difficult decisions to follow your character personality or because the character learned something (like studying).<br /> <br /> all these rewards are more narrative than mechanic, part of the fun is to see your character learn and change (not necessarly becoming more powerfull) and this is what i give exp for, my players want to have fun and thus they just try to roleplay at their best (ofc someone is better at doing it than others but that's no problem if you commit yourself) because they want to roleplay and not because i give them exp. Infact i usually give exp every 4-5 session that is often 1 month and half real life time.<br /> <br /> p.s. that's how my group handles exp in every game not only mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7038,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7038-nirgal","user":"Nirgal","date":". 10-19-2016, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7038-nirgal","name":"Nirgal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T10:31:52-07:00","id":989948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nirgal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=989934#post989934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i award exp for partecipating in events (you always learn at least something), for creative thinking or for anything that moves the story forward, for the introduction of interesting elements or even sidestories, for playing your character above the average making difficult decisions to follow your character personality or because the character learned something (like studying).</div> </div> </div> </div>These are all exactly the things that CofD give you beats for as written. You are just saying 'Mechanics' because they are in the book with a list of situations and how much they are worth. It isn't actually any different from what you are doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nirgal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=989934#post989934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">my players want to have fun and thus they just try to roleplay at their best (ofc someone is better at doing it than others but that's no problem if you commit yourself) because they want to roleplay and not because i give them exp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing about this system would change that, your players know that they get xp for roleplay, thats the same system, just without a name. You are trusting your players to not 'do it because of the XP', but you dont actually know whats in their heads. That trust doesn't evaporate becuse its written into the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":".  Fixing a quote error 10-19-2016, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T10:33:53-07:00","id":989953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AinSoph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=989927#post989927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If players need Willpower they can come up with a scene where they act out a Vice, and you can portray those consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>you see this for me is inconceivable. A character would never think &quot;i'm low on willpower let's get a dose or some sex to bring it up&quot;, because no one would ever think something like that. If a player came up with something like that usually the other players step in saying &quot;you are metagaming&quot; and the one with that idea &quot;you are right, ok&quot;. At the table less out-of-game thinking and talking there is better is.<br /> <br /> I understand that this is about style or how you see roleplaying and most of our way of playing isn't going to be fun for others but, what i see from the new system is that it tries to force a tons of rules that aren't needed and they are forced so hard that they are core of the system itself now, they aren't &quot;optional&quot; something you can ignore without problems if you want to. I find it symptomatic that to make room for all those rules the actual setting has been reduced so much that if you don't have the first ed. manuals you know almost nothing of the setting: i had to introduce a new player to our group after we switched for the second ed. and i had to point him to the old core rulebook for all the fluff because the new core book was seriously lacking.<br /> <br /> there are a lot of games that in their system incentivize the cooperation of players (if that is needed to be incentivized) but they don't do it by founding the entire ruleset on metagaming, one thing is giving direction to how you can play and cooperate to create interesting stories, even giving you the ability to introduce elements out of the blue (like many games do with certain points that can be spent to introduce narrative elements), another thing is saying: make your math and follow this equation and you will be roleplaying!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7038-nirgal","name":"Nirgal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T10:35:58-07:00","id":989954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nirgal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=989934#post989934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i reward exp by what i consider appropriate and considering how fast i want to make the players progress. i usually have the directive that what you earn in-game doesn't need exp coverage and what you get with exp needs in-game coverage, for ex: if you want a contact in the police departement go ahead and in-game find those contacts, if you find a way to achieve that you will get to write those contacts on your sheet; you want a safe place? go ahead and make arrangements, buy a house, find a good trusted security system installer etc; if you get a magical item in-game it's yours no need to spend exp to be able to use it.<br /> on the other hand if you get a magical object thx to exp you have to justify in-game why you have it, often such things are possible in the &quot;downtime&quot; between two stories or chapters.<br /> <br /> i award exp for partecipating in events (you always learn at least something), for creative thinking or for anything that moves the story forward, for the introduction of interesting elements or even sidestories, for playing your character above the average making difficult decisions to follow your character personality or because the character learned something (like studying).<br /> <br /> all these rewards are more narrative than mechanic, part of the fun is to see your character learn and change (not necessarly becoming more powerfull) and this is what i give exp for, my players want to have fun and thus they just try to roleplay at their best (ofc someone is better at doing it than others but that's no problem if you commit yourself) because they want to roleplay and not because i give them exp. Infact i usually give exp every 4-5 session that is often 1 month and half real life time.<br /> <br /> p.s. that's how my group handles exp in every game not only mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, to actually answer my question, you're saying, &quot;No, you haven't tried it.&quot;<br /> <br /> You should try it.<br /> <br /> It's super-great that you've managed to house-rule your way into half of the 2e system by yourself, but that is not what I was asking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T10:37:22-07:00","id":989956,"title":"","content":"I'm just gonna bow out of this conversation since I'm actually getting pretty worked up. I find your attitude dismissive at worst and elitist at best. I'm sure you don't intend it that way, but I think about the story and how my character fits in it as much as I think about what my character's thinking about. And you better believe that making decisions based on that out-of-character thinking is still roleplaying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T10:41:08-07:00","id":989957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=989948#post989948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> These are all exactly the things that CofD give you beats for as written. You are just saying 'Mechanics' because they are in the book with a list of situations and how much they are worth. It isn't actually any different from what you are doing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Nothing about this system would change that, your players know that they get xp for roleplay, thats the same system, just without a name. You are trusting your players to not 'do it because of the XP', but you dont actually know whats in their heads. That trust doesn't evaporate becuse its written into the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>i don't award exp for imposing a penalty on yourself and then removing it...<br /> more importantly players do not know how much exp they are going to get, if they are going to get it in the first place. exp is totally secondary and not being a known quantity players just can't plan to get it and can't play for it. Not that this is really needed because it depends on your style and what you are looking for in roleplaying, my problem is the fact that the game encourages you to think of exp and not the roleplay, it encourages you to act outside the game.<br /> <br /> to me it's quite irrelevant this kind of turn CoD has taken, the golden rule ofc always wins, i'm afraid that this approach is... &quot;non educational&quot; i don't know how to say it, but in short it doesn't pushes players toward actual roleplay but more to tabeltop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7038-nirgal","name":"Nirgal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T10:46:58-07:00","id":989959,"title":"","content":"It's collaborative storytelling. The system bribes players into making it difficult for their character because that makes for more interesting stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T10:50:02-07:00","id":989961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=989954#post989954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, to actually answer my question, you're saying, &quot;No, you haven't tried it.&quot;<br /> <br /> You should try it.<br /> <br /> It's super-great that you've managed to house-rule your way into half of the 2e system by yourself, but that is not what I was asking.</div> </div> </div> </div>depends on the story. often we don't even use exp and most of what you get to your sheet even when we use exp isn't bought with exp.<br /> generally what i wrote is the guidelines we use for every game with a long running chronicle were we prefer to give some freedom of choice in what fields a character develops outside the actual game.<br /> being that the reason we award exp for don't mean you get 1 exp for doing this, means players usually have certain points in the chronicle where they can buy what they belive is appropriate, it's just a conventional way of keeping the powerlevel clear for everyone. We had a campaign that lasted more than 1 year without the need to award exp (wasn't mage) but character developed just by playing and putting some improvements on the sheets when they made sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's collaborative storytelling. The system bribes players into making it difficult for their character because that makes for more interesting stories. </div> </div> </div>the point is the bribe. than can be argued that increasing the difficulty of things doesn't mean they get more interesting, often because then your narrator has to adjust things pro-players. Anyway you should try to make things interesting because you want to have fun not as a by product of getting exp, that's all i'm saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7038,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7038-nirgal","user":"Nirgal","date":". 10-19-2016, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7038-nirgal","name":"Nirgal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T10:59:41-07:00","id":989964,"title":"","content":"You don't like the thing. Okay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T11:44:10-07:00","id":989988,"title":"","content":"Alright, so this is a big philosophical split among much of the RPG community. It's been described in a lot of different ways in the past, with varying degrees of accuracy. &quot;Gamist&quot; vs. &quot;Simulationist&quot;, &quot;Director Stance&quot; vs. &quot;Actor Stance&quot;, &quot;Roll-playing&quot; vs. &quot;Role-playing&quot;, &quot;Metagaming&quot; vs... err... &quot;Not Metagaming&quot;, etc. What it comes down to is the fact that some people prefer players to make decisions exclusively based on in-character information, and some don't care if players use out-of-character information to help them make decisions. For some folks, if the player's desires and the character's desires are not in-sync 100% of the time, it breaks immersion and harms the experience. Chronicles of Darkness Second Edition is not the system for those people.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing, Chronicles of Darkness is a collaborative stoytelling system first and formost. That's why it's <i>called</i> &quot;The Storytelling System.&quot; The system priorities rules that get everyone involved in creating a dynamic and dramatically interesting horror story over preserving the synchronicity between player desires and character desires. It concedes that players will always make decisions based on out of character information. Like, literally it's impossible for human beings to ignore information they have access to when making a decision, because when you try to, you're still using that information to make your decision, you're just using it in the negative. e.g. &quot;Well, <i>I</i> know trolls are weak to fire, but does <i>my character</i> know that? Maybe I should cast magic missile instead of fireball&quot; is still a decision made based on the fact that you know, out-of-character, that fireball will be more effective against the troll. So, rather than trying to fight basic human psychology, Chronicles of Darkness works <i>with</i> it. Instead of asking players to pretend they don't know that going off alone to investigate a strange noise in a horror story is <i>always</i> a bad thing for the character who does it, and do it anyway because it's &quot;what my character would do&quot;, it just encourages the player to want to go off alone and investigate the strange noise, because that's what happens in horror stories and players can find a way to justify absolutely anything as in-character if it's something they want to do.<br /> <br /> Now, some people don't like that design philosophy. You're absolutely not alone in disliking 2e because of these kinds of mechanics, it's just that most folks who feel that way don't stick around these forums for very long, cause the vibe here is very 2e-centric. But, if you prefer to keep players' desires and characters' desires in-sync, that's fine. 2e won't be the system to satisfy that objective without a <i>lot</i> of house ruling, though. You may want to consider using 1e as a baseline and bringing over elements of 2e that you like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T11:45:53-07:00","id":989989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nirgal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=989953#post989953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> you see this for me is inconceivable. A character would never think &quot;i'm low on willpower let's get a dose or some sex to bring it up&quot;, because no one would ever think something like that. If a player came up with something like that usually the other players step in saying &quot;you are metagaming&quot; and the one with that idea &quot;you are right, ok&quot;. At the table less out-of-game thinking and talking there is better is.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Except that isn't at all how a character would actually behave if they were a real person. It is absolutely in-character and non-immersion breaking for someone who's feeling tapped out by life to indulge in the things that let them recover, which Vices fall squarely into both in game and in the real world. If anything it would be metagaming to <i>not</i> do it simply because you know there's a mechanical benefit attached. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T12:03:17-07:00","id":990007,"title":"","content":"Firstly, the obligatory quote, &quot;You keep using that word, I do not think it means what you think it means&quot;.<br /> <br /> Secondly, out of character, I've just had a nasty fight with some Seers, so bad did the fight go that two of my player group lost their characters. I'm completely out of will power, I'm down to a couple mana, and the ST just borrowed my sheet and then opened his note book to where he keeps his Praetorians. So, when he asks me what I'm doing, I say that my character is off to indulge his Vice. <br /> <br /> In character, a painful shit storm just rained down on me and my cabal. Henry and Victoria just bought it, took everything I had to survive and I know I didn't kill enough of the Exarchs hounds to keep them from trying to track me down and finish what they started. Now, I've always had a problem with drinking, kept it under control the last couple of years, but fuck it, I need a drink and damn the consequences. Maybe next turn of the wheel I'll have a better life. <br /> <br /> Now here, which one is the &quot;true&quot; motivation. Sure, I, the player wants some willpower to help me survive to game another day, but in game, Charles there is having a hell of a bad week, so bad, he wants to drink himself into oblivion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T12:08:40-07:00","id":990011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nirgal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=989934#post989934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i reward exp by what i consider appropriate and considering how fast i want to make the players progress. i usually have the directive that what you earn in-game doesn't need exp coverage and what you get with exp needs in-game coverage, for ex: if you want a contact in the police departement go ahead and in-game find those contacts, if you find a way to achieve that you will get to write those contacts on your sheet; you want a safe place? go ahead and make arrangements, buy a house, find a good trusted security system installer etc; if you get a magical item in-game it's yours no need to spend exp to be able to use it.<br /> on the other hand if you get a magical object thx to exp you have to justify in-game why you have it, often such things are possible in the &quot;downtime&quot; between two stories or chapters.<br /> <br /> i award exp for partecipating in events (you always learn at least something), for creative thinking or for anything that moves the story forward, for the introduction of interesting elements or even sidestories, for playing your character above the average making difficult decisions to follow your character personality or because the character learned something (like studying).<br /> <br /> all these rewards are more narrative than mechanic, part of the fun is to see your character learn and change (not necessarly becoming more powerfull) and this is what i give exp for, my players want to have fun and thus they just try to roleplay at their best (ofc someone is better at doing it than others but that's no problem if you commit yourself) because they want to roleplay and not because i give them exp. Infact i usually give exp every 4-5 session that is often 1 month and half real life time.<br /> <br /> p.s. that's how my group handles exp in every game not only mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like you run games in a manner very similar to myself. Story forward, focused heavily on the collective roleplay element over adherence to mechanical rigor. That's pretty hard to do, btw, and if you're pulling it off that's great. Honestly it sounds to me like you don't NEED all those rules. Everything you've said tells me you and your group have a strong dynamic, maybe strong enough that you can just ignore the stuff you don't like. That's kinda how the game is designed, too. Very few systems are so integral to play that they cannot be excised or downplayed. I run without Beats, never roll Integrity analogues (because I trust my players to know when they've hit a breaking point), and very rarely have to pull out Tilts or Conditions in any mechanical sense (again, the players handle the narrative effects all on their own), hell I've run a couple of sessions diceless because no one felt there was any need to roll. <br /> <br /> And there isn't anything wrong with any of that. The truth is that the system is just a crutch, a way of handling with dots and dice what may be difficult to achieve with pure narrative. But if that crutch gets in the way there is no shame in tossing it out the window.<br /> <br /> If you are interested in system tweaking, I'd actually recommend you check out the Storypath System Spoilers for Scion 2e. It is similar enough to CofD that many elements can be ported over, and is clearly laser focused on creating streamlined roleplaying experiences without getting too fiddly with dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T12:48:54-07:00","id":990045,"title":"","content":"My only problem with these extra mechanics is I can't remember to use these extra mechanics, often feel like there are too many things I need to remember, or reference and not enough quick reference. Still peeved at Demon, and Beast for having to look for the &quot;How many atavisms/demonic form&quot; because it's not in the character creation quick reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T13:18:44-07:00","id":990065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nirgal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=989953#post989953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a player came up with something like that usually the other players step in saying &quot;you are metagaming&quot; and the one with that idea &quot;you are right, ok&quot;. At the table less out-of-game thinking and talking there is better is</div> </div> </div> </div>Indulging in vice or seeking to fulfill a virtue as meta-gaming?? While the character may no think in terms &quot;vice&quot; and&quot;virtue&quot; let me assure you human beings, which characters are based off of, <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/InUniverseCatharsis\" target=\"_blank\">do seek to relieve stress and find meaning when they've reach their mental/emotional limits,</a> which is exactly what those mechanics represent. Willpower is essentially a track to measure mental and emotional limits of stress a character can withstand, which is why it uses the Resistance stat for Mental and Social attributes.<br /> <br /> Blowing off steam by indulgence or through seeking meaning reflects real life and is a profound <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CatharsisFactor\" target=\"_blank\">trope</a>.in storytelling. We, players and storytellers, are engaging in activities (many of us have virtues and vices which the hobby of gaming fulfills), it is where we seek catharsis even if we wouldn't label it as such. As a player you can be more aware of your character's motives than they are, and in most cases you <i>should </i>be more aware will be, as most characters like most people are not particularly self-aware.<br /> <br /> The example in the quote isn't necessarily good role play but seems to me to be a<u> lack of understanding of what mechanics represent, which gets in the way of good role play.</u><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nirgal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=989934#post989934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i reward exp by what i consider...<br /> <br /> ...in every game not only mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>This and the couple paragraphs of text between it, translates simple to 'no' for the question quoted in that post. I point this out because the lack of a simple answer before the explanation struck me as odd, thus worthy of pointing out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 10-20-2016, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T13:19:40-07:00","id":990066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nirgal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=989953#post989953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A character would never think &quot;i'm low on willpower let's get a dose or some sex to bring it up&quot;, because no one would ever think something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but &quot;Man, I'm stressed and I need a drink/hit/joint/smoke.&quot; or &quot;I'm all horned up right now.&quot; get said <i>all the time</i>. Current Willpower, like health, represents relative status---game indication of an in-game state.<br /> <br /> Low willpower means that you are more ruled by Id than ego than normal. A vice is tempting even when self destructive. A virtue is refreshing.<br /> <br /> Virtue and Vice represent the specific go-to impulses that a character's mind is prone to. If a character doesn't automatically <i>want</i> to indulge in some behavior when feeling weak or ground down, that simply <i>isn't</i> one of their vices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T23:07:30-07:00","id":990289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=990066#post990066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, but &quot;Man, I'm stressed and I need a drink/hit/joint/smoke.&quot; or &quot;I'm all horned up right now.&quot; get said <i>all the time</i>. Current Willpower, like health, represents relative status---game indication of an in-game state.<br /> <br /> Low willpower means that you are more ruled by Id than ego than normal. A vice is tempting even when self destructive. A virtue is refreshing.<br /> <br /> Virtue and Vice represent the specific go-to impulses that a character's mind is prone to. If a character doesn't automatically <i>want</i> to indulge in some behavior when feeling weak or ground down, that simply <i>isn't</i> one of their vices.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yup, can't remember how many times I went with &quot;can't do proper work. Just wanna get laid/do kinky stuff&quot;. (yes, Lusty would certainly be my vice). So real people do try to refresh themselves. They just think in direct terms do X -&gt; be refreshed. While in game it's do X -&gt; get WP -&gt; be refreshed","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T01:37:58-07:00","id":990336,"title":"","content":"It's like a vampire feeding when they get low on Vitae. In-game, they're hungry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T01:53:18-07:00","id":990346,"title":"","content":"I think aspirations were partly ment exactly for &quot;getting things in game&quot;<br /> <br /> Like say, you want to get contacs in the police. You put that as an Aspiration. Now you get beats for working towards that. After you get the exp you can use it to buy the merit. It requires a bit of abstraction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T12:38:27-07:00","id":990560,"title":"","content":"In my experience, the assumption that the existence of rules somehow inhibits roleplaying reveals a fundamental misunderstanding of the medium. In these games, rules are tools, not requirements. Just because the Social Maneuvering rules are there, for example, does not mean you have to bust them out for *every single* interaction where someone needs a favor from somebody else.<br /> <br /> Just last night I ran a session where one of the characters wanted someone to teleport him to another city to save himself a drive. If I wanted to, I could have figured out a number of doors, an impression level, and so on, but really? I didn't feel that would be helpful. So we just roleplayed it for five minutes, and eventually the guy gave the PC what he wanted, and sent him on his way. <br /> <br /> Come to think of it, based on how my group operates, I might never run into a situation where I think Social Maneuvering would be helpful. But I'm not so closed-minded that I'm going to resent their inclusion in the book. Simply put, if I don't like them? I don't use them. No need to judge other people who might.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12387-fourthdimensional","name":"FourthDimensional","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T12:43:48-07:00","id":990565,"title":"","content":"Poor Social Maneuvering. It really is a fantastic system with a bad case of looking clunkier on paper than it works out to be in play. Maybe some day I'll do an AP with the intention of spotlighting examples of how to use SM to good effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T12:47:04-07:00","id":990569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=990565#post990565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Poor Social Maneuvering. It really is a fantastic system with a bad case of looking clunkier on paper than it works out to be in play. Maybe some day I'll do an AP with the intention of spotlighting examples of how to use SM to good effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would read that AP. Hell, I'd help make that AP.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T12:49:32-07:00","id":990574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=990569#post990569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would read that AP. Hell, I'd help make that AP.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never done one before, but that's one I would be interested in doing. I don't have the time to commit to it right now, but I'll keep it in mind for the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T13:09:07-07:00","id":990583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=990574#post990574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've never done one before, but that's one I would be interested in doing. I don't have the time to commit to it right now, but I'll keep it in mind for the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here actually. I know this thread's in the mage subforum, but what gameline would you want to use for the AP?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T13:25:12-07:00","id":990592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FourthDimensional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=990560#post990560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my experience, the assumption that the existence of rules somehow inhibits roleplaying reveals a fundamental misunderstanding of the medium.</div> </div> </div> </div>This^<br /> <br /> The idea that 'role-play' means that there aren't rules for it sticks in my craw so bad. Especially since it implies that when you ARE using rules you aren't 'role-playing' any more. When my character attacks someone and I roll dice, I am still role-playing. When I use a spell and I roll dice, I am still role-playing. When I hunt for my Obsession or dive into a Vice, I am still role-playing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T13:33:41-07:00","id":990595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=990583#post990583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Same here actually. I know this thread's in the mage subforum, but what gameline would you want to use for the AP?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably either Vampire or Werewolf. They're the lines I'm most familiar with. Vampire has the advantage of being highly socially focused by default, but Werewolf has really tight focus and gives the opportunity to showcase Social interaction with spirits, which has some of its own quirks like starting at a Hostile Impression by default and needing to offer them Gathra.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, Werewolf would be a great excuse to dust off my Rockies update, which would put it in familiar territory for me... Hmm...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-20-2016, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T13:42:52-07:00","id":990603,"title":"","content":"I think 2e is very good at introducing mechanics that reinforce roleplay. I know &quot;enforce&quot; has negative connotations, and in a perfect world we wouldn't need Humanity because every player could perfectly roleplay their vampire's descent into monstrosity, but there's nothing wrong with using mechanics to support the sort of storytelling you want. A lot of these mechanics support actual, metaphysically powerful parts of what a character is and is becoming. Mage having an Obsession mechanic doesn't just mean &quot;your character should have a goal&quot;, it means that becoming a Mage, and the condition of being one, genuinely alters your soul and mind and causes you to inevitably obsess over mysteries and projects. <br /> <br /> Of course, you can always change or remove those mechanics. That's the beauty of ChroD. Take a look at Mirrors or the Chronicler's Guides, they have rules for adjusting mechanics to fit different kinds of stories and playstyles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T13:48:18-07:00","id":990608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=990595#post990595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably either Vampire or Werewolf. They're the lines I'm most familiar with. Vampire has the advantage of being highly socially focused by default, but Werewolf has really tight focus and gives the opportunity to showcase Social interaction with spirits, which has some of its own quirks like starting at a Hostile Impression by default and needing to offer them Gathra.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, Werewolf would be a great excuse to dust off my Rockies update, which would put it in familiar territory for me... Hmm...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T19:32:34-07:00","id":990758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=990565#post990565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Poor Social Maneuvering. It really is a fantastic system with a bad case of looking clunkier on paper than it works out to be in play. Maybe some day I'll do an AP with the intention of spotlighting examples of how to use SM to good effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, the main issue has always been the minimum time between rolls. I can't for the life of me think of a way to make that feel organic rather than forced. So I only ever use the option that takes just one roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T20:08:19-07:00","id":990771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=990758#post990758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, the main issue has always been the minimum time between rolls. I can't for the life of me think of a way to make that feel organic rather than forced. So I only ever use the option that takes just one roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, for me, this comes down to the way I resolve PC actions. When I ST, I ask the players to describe their characters' actions, and if a roll is necessary to determine the result of an action, I will ask them to do so. If a player asks &quot;can I make a Persuasion check&quot; or what have you, I ask them to tell me how they are attempting to persuade the other person, and say that if a check is needed, I will let them know. Then, I fall back on adjudication 101. If there is no chance of success, the action fails and I describe the result. If there is no chance of failure or no consequence for failure, the action succeeds and I describe the result. If there is a reasonable chance of success, a reasonable chance of failure, and consequences for failure, I ask for the player to make an appropriate roll, and describe the results of the action based on the results of the roll. In the case of Social actions, Doors only come into play in the third scenario; when the PC is asking something of an NPC that there is a chance they would be willing to agree to, and a chance they would refuse (failing to open a Door being the consequence for failure). Based on the player's approach, I will determine an appropriate dice pool and ask them to roll it once during the interval based on the Impression. If the PC continues to press the matter, the NPC will react like anyone does when someone tries to rush them into a decision - let them know that they are considering it, but need some time to think, and try to change the subject. If they still continue to push, that's a Forcing Doors roll. However, due to how easy it is to achieve an Excellent or Perfect impression by the book, and the fact that time in interaction scenes is often pretty abstract, making it pretty easy to get 2 or 3 half hour intervals in a single interaction scene, and most NPCs are going to have a base 2 or 3 Doors, it's usually possible to open them all without needing to Force Doors or come back later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-20-2016, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T04:42:49-07:00","id":990895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=990595#post990595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably either Vampire or Werewolf. They're the lines I'm most familiar with. Vampire has the advantage of being highly socially focused by default, but Werewolf has really tight focus and gives the opportunity to showcase Social interaction with spirits, which has some of its own quirks like starting at a Hostile Impression by default and needing to offer them Gathra.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, Werewolf would be a great excuse to dust off my Rockies update, which would put it in familiar territory for me... Hmm...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's perfect for me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T05:04:38-07:00","id":990904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=990569#post990569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would read that AP. Hell, I'd help make that AP.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would read that AP, too. I find it a very good and useful idea ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T09:55:05-07:00","id":991002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=990758#post990758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me, the main issue has always been the minimum time between rolls. I can't for the life of me think of a way to make that feel organic rather than forced. So I only ever use the option that takes just one roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi. I've seen this a few times and I've written a big thing about it. It's in my signature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T19:31:26-07:00","id":991225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nirgal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay#post989861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am i the only one feeling that this new course of cod is going too much on the gamist side of the spectrum?</div> </div> </div> </div>No you arent. Taking from each point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TelperionST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=989874#post989874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Aspirations and Obsessions</b><br /> I think these are a great addition to the game. These are neatly divided into long and short-term goals that give information to the Storyteller. What are the players interested in? How are they going to go about fulfilling these goals? What are they aiming at in the short-term (this or the next session) or in the long-term (half a dozen to a dozen sessions from now)? I ask my players to create a storyline of their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally this is the core of why i, personally, dislike the obsesions and their like. Instead of making a whole mechanic, why not talk....like adults about what the player and the ST want. It seems to me as an in-game solution for a out-of-game problem which is an awful tendency dating owod.<br /> <br /> However since playing with more wod dms, i have found the &quot;speaking like adults&quot; is an option rarely so maybe its necessary than it though.<br /> <br /> The other part of my dislike of 2ed is their tendency of defining how your character feels, like all werewolf &quot;think in terms of hunting&quot; or all mages are &quot;obsessive&quot;. To me it feels restrictive as i like npcs who are agaisnt type.<br /> <br /> <b>Condition, beats and tilts</b><br /> <br /> Conditions and tilts are meh. I mean its an obvious......borrowing, to Fate aspects and i guess there is an incentive for PC to remember them. Conditions are also a way to make &quot;flaws&quot; more integrated into the games as before i never saw any players taking on flaws (nwod). Its one of those &quot;perception beats reality&quot; kind of things, flaws (nwod) on the long run give more XP than Flaws (owod) but as owods had inmediate effect (and more interesting flaws) i seen people pick more flaws in owod over never picking up flaws in NWoD. Plus there was always that little chance the DM would forget about your flaws and you will feel cool about &quot;gaming&quot; the &quot;system&quot; which wasnt possible in Nwod.<br /> <br /> Conditions as flaws are more integrated and tend to come up more as players dont tend to see them as &quot;flaws&quot; but more &quot;everyday&quot; mechanic that they already interact constantly.<br /> <br /> Tilts are effect with fancy names, nothing much to them.<br /> <br /> And beats for dramatic failures are a band-aid in a broken mechanic. Dramatic failures could almost never happened unless a player wanted it (saw a chance die, decide for that course of action and even then it was a 1/10), or a house rules was in play that once you saw the dicepool there were no backsies.....and even then 1/10.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=990758#post990758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, the main issue has always been the minimum time between rolls. I can't for the life of me think of a way to make that feel organic rather than forced. So I only ever use the option that takes just one roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way i handle it is.<br /> <br /> Is this a short term social situation (ex: convincing the bouncer to let you in)?<br /> <br /> Yes? Then 1 attribute + skill constested roll and continue<br /> <br /> Is this a long term social situation (ex: convincing a dude to let you borrow his house for the weekend)?<br /> <br /> Yes? The social door system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 10-21-2016, 10:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T12:44:34-07:00","id":991957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nirgal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay#post989861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Roleplay becomes a mechanic that is even rewarded mechanically with exp: obsessions are just a way to keep control of players and force them to do things that are compatible with the narrator storyline</div> </div> </div> </div>Are YOU setting their Obsessions? In that case you're doing it wrong. Obsessions are personal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nirgal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay#post989861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i can see how this can help gamists and inexperienced narrators but i think that is a way to transform a roleplaying game into a boardgame, more on the subject conditions and tilts... seriously how are needed 10 pages of those things? to keep track you even have cards...</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no real complaints with the Conditions system except for the fact that there are a lot of them and they're hard to all remember until you need them. I'm also not super clear on when they're needed versus when they're not, but I like them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nirgal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay#post989861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">then players start to think that they have to do something because they have an obsession...</div> </div> </div> </div>They're wrong. An obsession is up to you to pursue or not as you feel you need.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nirgal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay#post989861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">then comes the social conflict rule system... Seriously what's the need of an in depth rule system to decide the outcome of roleplay? A character needs to convince someone and to do so what he does? start rolling diece... a chance to roleplay becomes a chance to roll dice. Since your character is good at speaking you can brain off and let dice do the talking...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's to give meaning to social skills and allow players who aren't good at convincing people a chance to do something. Also, you should be roleplaying WHILE doing so and possibly handing out bonuses for doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T16:01:39-07:00","id":992081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=991957#post991957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are YOU setting their Obsessions? In that case you're doing it wrong. Obsessions are personal.</div> </div> </div> </div>While one can argue that the DM has to vet the obsessions, for example if someone came to with a PC with &quot;urathas&quot; as obsession i would tell him &quot;change that one i dont do crossover games of any kind&quot; but besides that you are right <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7038-nirgal\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7038\" data-vbnamecard=\"7038\">Nirgal</a> complain is confusing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=991957#post991957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're wrong. An obsession is up to you to pursue or not as you feel you need.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you expland on this because that phrase makes no sense. If its up to the players to pursue them, then how its not as they feel they need to pursue them?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T23:27:18-07:00","id":992277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=992081#post992081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you expland on this because that phrase makes no sense. If its up to the players to pursue them, then how its not as they feel they need to pursue them?</div> </div> </div> </div>A player is not FORCED to pursue their obsessions. The game does not directly PUNISH them for doing so. Failing to do so does deny you a source of beats and mana, yes, but no more than ignoring any other source of adversity and the pursuit of magical interest. Just like in real life, you can turn away from something that obsesses you.<br /> <br /> If your players ever say &quot;I can't do this, I have to follow my obsession,&quot; simply remind them that &quot;No, you can choose not to if you feel that's what you would do in this circumstance.&quot;<br /> It's as simple as that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T03:11:11-07:00","id":992309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989861-too-many-rules-too-few-roleplay?p=992277#post992277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A player is not FORCED to pursue their obsessions. The game does not directly PUNISH them for doing so. Failing to do so does deny you a source of beats and mana, yes, but no more than ignoring any other source of adversity and the pursuit of magical interest. Just like in real life, you can turn away from something that obsesses you.<br /> <br /> If your players ever say &quot;I can't do this, I have to follow my obsession,&quot; simply remind them that &quot;No, you can choose not to if you feel that's what you would do in this circumstance.&quot;<br /> It's as simple as that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I understand now, thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}